+# PAYESS-01 — Mijn salaris V1 Acceptance
+
+- Run date: 2026-10-13
+- Classification: **CONTROLLED** (AA-LEAN-02)
+- Result: **PARTIAL — LOCAL IMPLEMENTATION GREEN; AUTHENTICATED TEST ACCEPTANCE OPEN**
+- Feature branch: `work/PAYESS-01-20261013`
+- Code commit: `e0fc0e97f843d744097687b5db9ff26dd63b8bd5`
+
+## 1. Executive Summary
+
+Implemented a responsive employee salary dashboard and one shared payslip list for My Salary and the employee dossier. The server selects only the authenticated employee’s scoped, fully finalized periods. The dedicated employee PDF route is read-only and does not call the HR Admin preview route. Local automated gates passed. Authenticated TEST acceptance was not run because the available Test Auth flow performs remote Supabase sign-out/sign-in, while this task excludes remote writes.
+
+| ID | Area | What broke | Why | Fix | Regression | Result |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| PAYESS-01 | `/my-salary`, employee payslips and Payroll PDF access | Existing self-service read model exposed one period; employee and admin payslip surfaces were separate | No multi-period self read model or employee-scoped Payroll PDF response existed | Added scoped period projection, dashboard, read-only period PDF endpoint, and shared imported/Payroll payslip list | 8 focused files / 55 tests; full HR suite; local anonymous desktop/mobile route check | PARTIAL — authenticated TEST browser acceptance remains open |
+
+## 2. Coverage
+
+Dashboard period selection, gross/net chart, previous available period comparison, component changes, explanations, empty/history states, and unified imported/Payroll payslip grouping were implemented. Payroll statements and generated PDFs are only exposed for complete `CONCEPT → REVIEWED → FINALIZED` lifecycle records. Imported PDFs continue to use the existing storage and secure download service.
+
+## 3. Role Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Evidence | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| Employee reads own finalized salary | Authorization service test | GREEN |
+| Request supplies another employee ID / repository returns another employee artifact | Service tests verify self identity and artifact owner | DENIED |
+| Different tenant, HR group or administration | Scope mismatch tests | DENIED |
+| Missing self salary permission or dossier `salary:read` | Authorization tests; repositories are not queried | DENIED |
+| Missing imported payslip `payslip:read` or out-of-scope document ID | Payslip service tests | DENIED |
+| Concept-only or incomplete lifecycle | Statement and PDF service tests | HIDDEN / DENIED |
+| PDF requested for another employee or unavailable period | PDF service and response tests | DENIED / NOT FOUND |
+| Authenticated live employee role | No Test Auth request was submitted | OPEN |
+
+## 4. Functional Results
+
+- Actual persisted periods only; tests cover 0, 1, multiple periods and gaps without inventing months.
+- Gross and net trend, period filter, tooltips, euro/percentage comparison and changed saved components.
+- Breakdown explanations preserve missing/unverified pension and calculation warnings; missing values are not presented as zero.
+- One year/month-grouped list shares existing imported payslip references and period-based Payroll PDF links across My Salary and the dossier. No second PDF store or automatic archive writes were added.
+- New Payroll documents are read-only and available only after finalization. Existing stored PDFs are returned unchanged; rendering is transient when needed.
+
+## 5. Negative/Security Results
+
+Unit/service tests cover self identity, client-supplied employee ID, artifact ownership, tenant/HR-group/administration scope, missing permissions, lifecycle state, unavailable periods and another employee’s PDF. The response contains an allow-listed statement projection; tests assert that source payloads, hashes and traces are absent. The dedicated period route derives employee identity from the authenticated server context and uses no caller-selected run ID. The HR Admin preview route is not reused.
+
+These are mocked/service-level assertions. No authenticated live API probe or TEST data readback was performed.
+
+## 6. Mobile/Responsive Results
+
+The local `/my-salary` request redirected to `/login?next=%2Fmy-salary` at 1440×900 and 390×844. The anonymous login page rendered at both sizes. This proves the route’s anonymous gate only; authenticated dashboard layout, chart interaction, document viewer, download and browser console/network acceptance remain open.
+
+## 7. Data/DB Readback
+
+No migration, schema change, salary run, component activation, payslip archive write or remote application data mutation was performed. No authenticated Payroll database readback was performed. The browser used only an anonymous local route request; the Test Auth sign-in endpoint was not submitted.
+
+## 8. Quality Gates
+
+- Focused feature/security tests: 8 files, 55 tests passed.
+- Full HR suite: 630 files passed, 4 skipped; 3,027 tests passed, 8 skipped.
+- HR suite TypeScript, changed-file ESLint, i18n parity (43 namespaces), and `git diff --check`: passed.
+- Production build: passed; 323 routes generated and the Payroll client-boundary scan passed for 163 assets.
+- The build reported an existing tracing warning around runtime logo-file discovery in the shared PDF renderer. It did not fail the build and was not changed in this feature.
+
+## 9. Fixed During Run
+
+No unrelated defects were changed. The requested feature adds a bounded multi-period self projection and separate employee PDF access while preserving existing permissions and finalization requirements.
+
+## 10. ENVIRONMENT-GATED
+
+The exact-commit authenticated TEST employee browser matrix and saved-data/PDF readback are open. The supported local Test Auth flow calls Supabase sign-out/sign-in, which would perform a remote Auth operation outside the no-remote-writes boundary. No isolated Preview backend was used. The local anonymous route check does not substitute for employee acceptance.
+
+## 11. PRODUCT DECISIONS
+
+- Empty history stays empty; only periods returned from stored Payroll data appear.
+- Unknown tax/pension inputs remain visibly unverified, not estimated.
+- Imported PDF storage is unchanged; both screens use the same document source reference.
+- Payroll PDF access is self-only, period-addressed, finalized-only and read-only.
+
+## 12. NOT FIXED
+
+- Authenticated live employee, tenant/administration and document download flows are unverified; next action is a controlled acceptance run against an approved isolated TEST/Preview backend with existing synthetic identities.
+- `origin/main` advanced from the task’s verified baseline `73cb370539770711544637962c4e897ea4cd6265` to `f7db482b19b81d9c5aa5517c66394faa5f628e1b` with PAYLAB-UX-01 during this work. That commit was intentionally kept out per scope. Before integration, reconcile the feature against the then-current main under the approved integration flow.
+
+## 13. LESSONS/PATTERNS
+
+The repository’s local runtime launcher passed preflight when pointed at the existing central TEST config without printing or copying its contents. The browser login path was inspected but not submitted. A CLI browser launch hit the Windows Chrome Crashpad pipe failure; the local anonymous desktop/mobile route check was completed in the Codex in-app browser instead.
+
+## 14. Commits/Remote Head
+
+- Code commit: `e0fc0e97f843d744097687b5db9ff26dd63b8bd5`.
+- Baseline at worktree creation: `73cb370539770711544637962c4e897ea4cd6265`.
+- `origin/main` at report time: `f7db482b19b81d9c5aa5517c66394faa5f628e1b`.
+- No merge, deployment, migration or TEST release was performed.
+
+## 15. Final Verdict
+
+**PARTIAL.** Implementation and local code gates are green. CONTROLLED authenticated TEST acceptance remains open for the employee’s actual saved history and both payslip sources, including download and the negative scope matrix. This candidate is not ready to claim TEST release.
